and loses all access. | Must | AC-021 |

## 8. Business rules

| ID | Rule | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| BR-001 | All members of a company can view all of its notes, versions, action items, and transcripts; nobody outside 
the company can. | Notes are company memory (r1 q4). |
| BR-002 | Any member can create a note in any space of their company, including private spaces. | Notes can be 
written after the meeting (r2 q11). |
| BR-003 | Edit rights: author, current participants, company admins. Delete rights: author, company admins. | r1 q5, 
r2 q11. |
| BR-004 | Action items: note editors create/edit/delete; editors and the assignee toggle completion. | The assignee 
closes their own work (r2 q8). |
| BR-005 | Participants and assignees must be active members of the note's company. | Prevents cross-company 
references. |
| BR-006 | AI suggestions never become assignments or stored content without explicit user confirmation. | Avoids 
wrong attributions (r1 q12). |
| BR-007 | Each save creates one immutable version; restore creates a new version; action items are current-state 
only. | r1 q8, r2 q10. |
| BR-008 | The daily limit applies to every company, counts only successful drafts (including reprocessing), and is 
adjustable by admins from 1 to 200. | Cost and abuse protection (r1 q11, r2 q4). |
| BR-009 | Only admins configure AI; the API key is write-only from the browser's perspective and is stored encrypted 
on the server. | r2 q1, q3. |
| BR-010 | One transcript per note; a new upload replaces the stored text; the stored transcript is visible to every 
note viewer. | r1 q13, r2 q12. |
| BR-011 | A save based on an outdated version is rejected. | No silent overwrite (r1 q18). |
| BR-012 | AI access uses API keys only; no subscription credentials are requested, stored, or proxied. | Anthropic 
policy; OpenAI sign-in not available (r3). |

## 9. Data and integrations

### Data inputs

- Note fields, participants, rich-text content, action items, transcript files (.txt/.vtt/.srt, UTF-8 text, â‰¤1 MB).
- Admin AI settings: provider, API key, model, reasoning level, daily limit.

### Data outputs

- Stored notes, versions, action items, transcripts, AI settings (key encrypted).
- AI drafts (transient until saved).
- Search results with excerpts; downloaded .md files.

### Integrations

- Anthropic Messages API (official SDK), OpenAI API (official SDK), Kimi (Moonshot) and GLM (Zhipu/Z.ai) through their 
OpenAI-compatible endpoints. All calls are server-side from authenticated API routes.
- Supabase Postgres (RLS, full-text search), Supabase Auth.
- The existing `meeting_notes` and `meeting_note_action_items` tables and `IMeetingNoteRepository` are reused and 
extended (for example, `summary` becomes optional for manual notes, and `room_id` no longer cascades on space 
deletion).

## 10. Constraints and assumptions

### Constraints

- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase Postgres/Auth/RLS, TanStack Query, shadcn/ui, following AGENTS.md 
(server client in routes, `auth.getUser()`, `users.id` vs `users.supabase_uid`, roles `admin|member`).
- API keys never reach client code, logs, error messages, or reports; transcript text is not logged.
- AI calls only from the server; the browser never calls a provider.
- Size limits: title â‰¤200 chars; content â‰¤100,000 chars; â‰¤50 participants; â‰¤100 action items per note; 
transcript â‰¤1 MB.
- UI in the app's current language (English); AI summary in the transcript's language.
- Migrations are written and applied locally during the phase; they are applied to the online database 
`vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` only at phase end with the owner's explicit authorization; rollout order is migrations then 
app, rollback is app first.
- Only integration and E2E tests (no unit tests); one test process at a time; one final Chrome-only E2E run.

### Assumptions

- The owner creates an OpenAI platform API key (billed separately from ChatGPT Plus/Pro) for the final test against 
the real provider (confirmed r3).
- Automated tests use a local fake AI server compatible with the provider APIs (confirmed r2 q17).

## 11. Edge cases and failure modes

| Case | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| Two editors save the same note concurrently | The later save is rejected with a conflict warning showing the newer 
version (FR-007). |
| Empty / >1 MB / wrong extension / binary file | Rejected before AI, clear message, nothing saved, not counted 
(FR-013). |
| .vtt/.srt with cue numbers and timestamps | Stripped; speaker names kept (FR-014). |
| Provider error, timeout, refusal, invalid key | Note and transcript stay saved; error + "Try again"; not counted 
(FR-020). |
| User leaves the page while processing | Draft discarded; not counted (FR-021). |
| AI suggests a name matching no member or several members | Item left unassigned for the user to choose (FR-017). |
| Daily limit reached | Processing refused with limit and reset time (FR-024). |
| No AI configured | Manual notes work; AI disabled with message; admin sees settings link (FR-023). |
| Space deleted | Notes kept, labelled "Space removed" (FR-027). |
| Participant/assignee leaves the company | Shown as "Former member"; no access (FR-028). |
| Assignee is not a note editor | Can toggle completion of their item only (BR-004). |
| Restore of an old version | New version created; action items unchanged (FR-009). |
| Transcript contains instructions aimed at the AI | Treated as data; output limited to the draft fields; suggested 
assignees resolved only against the company member list. |
| Pasted content with scripts or `javascript:` links | Removed by sanitization (FR-002). |
| Member of company A requests a note, version, item, search, or setting of company B | Not found / denied (BR-001, 
SM-3). |
| Non-admin calls the AI settings route | Denied (BR-009). |

## 12. Security, privacy, compliance, and abuse considerations

- RLS on every new or changed table, comparing `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text` and scoping by company; 
API routes resolve the application user by `supabase_uid`.
- API keys stored encrypted at rest, readable only by server code, never returned (only a mask), never logged.
- Rich text sanitized on write and render; Markdown export escapes content so it cannot inject HTML when rendered 
elsewhere.
- Transcript text is sent to a third-party provider only after the notice naming that provider; the admin's provider 
choice (including providers hosted outside Brazil/US) is the company's decision.
- Prompt-injection resistance: transcript is passed as data; output parsed against a fixed schema; any field outside 
the schema is discarded.
- Abuse: daily limit per company; size limits; server-side validation of every limit.
- Subscription credentials (Claude, ChatGPT) are never requested or stored.

## 13. Accessibility, localization, and usability considerations

- Editor, version list, review step, and dialogs are keyboard-operable with visible focus and labelled controls 
(Radix/shadcn primitives).
- Clear progress state while processing; errors state what happened and what to do.
- UI strings in English, matching the app; summary language follows the transcript.
- Interactive elements inside clickable cards follow the AGENTS.md interaction rules.

## 14. Acceptance criteria

- AC-001 (FR-001, FR-003, FR-005, BR-002): Given a member of company A, when they create a note in a space with title, 
date, two participants, and formatted content, then it appears first in that space's Notes tab and opens showing all 
fields.
- AC-002 (FR-001, BR-005): Given a title of 201 chars, content above 100,000 chars, 51 participants, or a participant 
from another company, when saving, then the save is rejected with a message and nothing is stored.
- AC-003 (FR-002): Given content containing a script tag and a `javascript:` link, when saved and viewed, then no 
script runs and the link is removed or neutralized.
- AC-004 (FR-006, BR-003): Given a note authored by user X with participant Y, when Y and an admin edit it, then both 
saves succeed; when a non-participant member Z tries to edit (UI or direct API call), then it is denied and Z sees no 
edit control.
- AC-005 (FR-007, BR-011): Given two sessions open the same note version, when both save different content, then the 
first succeeds and the second gets a conflict warning showing the first's content, and the first's content is not 
overwritten.
- AC-006 (FR-008, FR-009, BR-007): Given a note saved three times, when a viewer opens history, then three versions 
show author and time; when an editor restores version 1, then a fourth version equals version 1's fields and the 
action items are unchanged.
- AC-007 (FR-010, BR-003): Given a note with versions, items, and a transcript, when the author confirms delete, then 
the note, versions, items, and transcript are gone; when a participant who is not the author or an admin tries to 
delete, then it is denied.
- AC-008 (FR-011, BR-004): Given a note editor, when they add an item with description, assignee, and due date, then 
it is shown; when the assignee (not an editor) toggles completion, then it succeeds; when the assignee tries to edit 
the description or delete, then it is denied.
- AC-009 (FR-011): Given a note with 100 items, when adding a 101st or an item with an empty description, then it is 
rejected.
- AC-010 (FR-012, FR-015, FR-016, FR-018, FR-019, BR-006, BR-010): Given a configured provider (fake AI server in 
automated tests), when a member uploads a valid .txt to create a note, then a notice names the provider, a draft with 
summary and suggested items appears, and nothing is stored until save; after editing the summary, rejecting one item 
and accepting another, saving stores exactly the edited summary, the accepted item, and the transcript; reprocessing 
returns a new draft and leaves the stored summary unchanged until saved; attaching a transcript to an existing note 
replaces the previous one.
- AC-011 (FR-013): Given an empty file, a 1.1 MB file, a .pdf renamed .txt, or a .docx, when uploading, then each is 
rejected with a message, no AI call is made, nothing is stored, and the daily count is unchanged.
- AC-012 (FR-014): Given a .vtt and a .srt with cue numbers, timestamps, and speaker names, when processed, then the 
text sent to the provider contains no cue numbers or timestamps and keeps the speaker names.
- AC-013 (FR-017, BR-006): Given a draft suggesting "Ana" when one active member is Ana, "Bruno" when two members 
match, and "Carla" when none does, then Ana is pre-linked and Bruno's and Carla's items are unassigned.
- AC-014 (FR-004, FR-025, BR-001, SM-2, SM-3): Given 1,000 notes in company A and notes in company B containing the 
same words, when a member of A searches an accented word without the accent, with space and period filters, then only 
matching notes of A within the filters are returned, ranked, with excerpts, and the first page returns within 1 second 
locally; company B's notes never appear.
- AC-015 (FR-004): Given the dashboard, when the member clicks "AI Meeting Notes", then the Meetings page opens.
- AC-016 (FR-020, FR-021, FR-024, BR-008): Given the provider returns an error, times out, refuses, or rejects the 
key, then the note and transcript stay saved, an error with "Try again" appears, and the daily count is unchanged; 
given the user navigates away mid-processing, then no draft is stored and the count is unchanged; given the company 
reached its limit, then processing is refused with the limit and reset time.
- AC-017 (FR-022, BR-009): Given an admin, when they save provider, key, model, reasoning level, and limit 50, then 
the settings persist, the key is shown only masked, and no API response or page ever contains the key; given a member, 
when calling the settings route, then it is denied; given limit 0 or 201, then it is rejected.
- AC-018 (FR-023): Given no provider configured, when a member opens a note, then manual editing works and AI controls 
are disabled with "An admin needs to configure AI"; an admin additionally sees a link to settings.
- AC-019 (FR-005, FR-026): Given a note with formatted content, summary, items, and transcript, when exported without 
the option, then the .md contains title, date, space, participants, Markdown content, summary, and items but no 
transcript; with the option ticked, the transcript is included.
- AC-020 (FR-027): Given a space with notes, when the space is deleted, then its notes remain on the Meetings page and 
in search, labelled "Space removed".
- AC-021 (FR-028): Given a participant and assignee who leaves the company, then the note shows them as "Former 
member" and they can no longer read the note.
- AC-022 (SM-1, BR-012): Given the owner's real OpenAI API key configured on the deployed or locally run app against 
the online database, when processing a one-hour fictional transcript, then a draft appears within 60 seconds; at no 
point is a subscription login requested.
- AC-023 (SM-3, BR-001, BR-009): Given two companies, when a member of each attempts direct API and database access to 
the other's notes, versions, items, transcripts, search, and AI settings, then every attempt returns nothing or is 
denied.

## 15. Test strategy

- Levels: integration and E2E only (AGENTS.md). No unit tests; no mocking of Supabase, repositories, or the code under 
test.
- Integration (Vitest against local Supabase): RLS and route authorization per role and company (AC-004, AC-007, 
AC-008, AC-017, AC-021, AC-023); validation limits (AC-002, AC-009, AC-011); version creation and conflict (AC-005, 
AC-006); transcript normalization (AC-012); assignee matching (AC-013); limit counting and failure non-counting 
(AC-016); search correctness, isolation, and timing with 1,000 seeded notes (AC-014); space deletion (AC-020); key 
never returned (AC-017).
- External AI provider: replaced in automated tests only, by a local fake server speaking the provider APIs, selected 
by environment configuration, with fixed responses and scripted failures (error, timeout, refusal, invalid key). 
Database, RLS, routes, and UI stay real.
- E2E (Playwright, two accounts): manual note lifecycle, editing rights, conflict, history/restore, action items with 
assignee completion, transcript â†’ review â†’ save, AI-disabled state, admin settings, search, export download, 
sanitization (AC-001, AC-003â€“AC-008, AC-010, AC-015, AC-018, AC-019).
- Test data: fictional transcripts in .txt/.vtt/.srt, Portuguese and English, including speaker names, accents, and 
malformed files. No real personal data.
- Cadence: per task type-check + lint; per block type-check, lint, DB integration suite when server code changed; one 
final Chrome-only E2E run of all new specs plus the full regression suite, zero retries; one test process at a time.
- Owner test: AC-022 with a real provider key against the online database after the migrations are applied.

## 16. Validation and launch checklist

- All Must FRs and AC-001..AC-023 have evidence in TRACK.
- Adversarial reviews passed at SPEC, PLAN, each block, and final.
- Type-check, lint, build, DB integration suite, final E2E run green.
- Migrations listed with state: written locally, applied locally, applied to `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` (after 
authorization, catalog read back, smoke check), app deployed.
- ROADMAP updated: Phase 6 status; MEET-08 moved to Phase 7.
- Owner acceptance test (AC-022) passed.

## 17. Open questions

Non-blocking, resolved during planning:

- Exact curated model and reasoning-level list per provider.
- Rich-text editor library and stored format.
- Key encryption mechanism (for example, Supabase Vault or application-level encryption with a server-only secret).
- Day boundary for the daily limit (default proposal: UTC calendar day, shown to the user in local time).
Status: active

