 202: ## 12. Security, privacy, compliance, and abuse considerations
 203: 
 204: - RLS on every new or changed table, comparing `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text` and scoping by 
company; API routes resolve the application user by `supabase_uid`.
 205: - API keys stored encrypted at rest, readable only by server code, never returned (only a mask), never logged.
 206: - Rich text sanitized on write and render; Markdown export escapes content so it cannot inject HTML when 
rendered elsewhere.
 207: - Transcript text is sent to a third-party provider only after the notice naming that provider; the admin's 
provider choice (including providers hosted outside Brazil/US) is the company's decision.
 208: - Prompt-injection resistance: transcript is passed as data; output parsed against a fixed schema; any field 
outside the schema is discarded.
 209: - Abuse: daily limit per company; size limits; server-side validation of every limit.
 210: - Subscription credentials (Claude, ChatGPT) are never requested or stored.
 211: 
 212: ## 13. Accessibility, localization, and usability considerations
 213: 
 214: - Editor, version list, review step, and dialogs are keyboard-operable with visible focus and labelled controls 
(Radix/shadcn primitives).
 215: - Clear progress state while processing; errors state what happened and what to do.
 216: - UI strings in English, matching the app; summary language follows the transcript.
 217: - Interactive elements inside clickable cards follow the AGENTS.md interaction rules.
