**Verdict: REVISION REQUIRED.**

1. **H1 — High — FR-021, FR-024, BR-008: cancellation bypasses cost protection.**  
   **Scenario (browser/network):** A member starts processing, leaves after billable provider work begins, and 
repeats. FR-021 guarantees an unchanged counter, allowing unlimited company expenditure. Paid processing can produce 
no visible output. [OpenAI documentation](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/reasoning).  
   **Evidence:** [SPEC:119](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:119), [owner 
cancellation answer:91](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:91).  
   **Fix:** Add an **owner-approved** dispatch/attempt budget independent of successful-draft counting: cancellation 
after provider dispatch cannot replenish that budget. Changing cancellation counting instead also requires owner 
confirmation; it contradicts the recorded answer.

2. **H2 — High — FR-024, BR-008, AC-016: quota admission and settlement are undefined.**  
   **Scenario (concurrency/network/crash):** At 19/20, several requests independently pass the limit check and call 
the provider. A retried POST can produce another billed request; a crash between provider success and counter update 
loses accounting. AC-016 never asserts successful increments.  
   **Evidence:** [SPEC:122](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:122), 
[AC-016:236](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:236).  
   **Fix:** Require atomic company/day reservations before dispatch, admission against successful plus reserved usage, 
request idempotency, and crash recovery. Define “successful draft” as validated generation, independent of saving the 
note. Confirm the day boundary and test competing requests, retries, reset, reprocessing, and settings changes.

3. **H3 — High — FR-027, BR-001/003, §9: retained notes lack durable company and creator identity.**  
   **Scenario (real user):** An admin deletes a space. `room_id` is currently NOT NULL, so SET NULL fails; retaining a 
nullable row still makes existing note/item RLS deny access because both policies join through the deleted space. The 
schema also has only `edited_by`, which cannot establish the original author.  
   **Evidence:** 
[baseline:643](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183000_baseline_core_schema.sql:643), 
[RLS:256](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183139_enable_core_table_rls.sql:256).  
   **Fix:** Specify immutable, server-derived note company and creator identities using application UUIDs; nullable 
`room_id` with SET NULL; authorization/search through the retained company identity. Define company-deletion behavior 
and an owner-approved legacy-author policy—never infer creator from last editor.

4. **H4 — High — FR-015/022, §12: provider notice can become stale before dispatch.**  
   **Scenario (concurrency):** A member sees “Anthropic”; an admin changes the provider to GLM; processing reads the 
latest settings and sends the transcript to GLM without the promised notice. Mid-processing key/model changes also 
have no defined behavior.  
   **Evidence:** [FR-015:113](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:113), [privacy 
notice:207](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:207).  
   **Fix:** Bind the notice/start request to a settings revision. Reject stale revisions before dispatch and show the 
new provider notice. Snapshot the provider/key/model configuration for an admitted request; prohibit silent fallback 
and require a refreshed notice for subsequent retries.

5. **M1 — Medium — BR-003/004/005, FR-006/009/011: authorization-sensitive mutation paths are underspecified.**  
   **Scenario (real member):** A viewer inserts themselves into participants before authorization checks the resulting 
list. An assignee uses a broadly permitted item UPDATE to change description, assignee, or parent note. An existing 
participant grants another viewer editing rights through participant editing or restore.  
   **Evidence:** [business rules:134](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:134), 
[RLS requirement:204](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:204). RLS alone does not 
restrict writable columns. [Supabase 
documentation](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/postgres/column-level-security).  
   **Fix:** Require authorization against committed **pre-change** membership and participants, enforced at API and 
database/RPC boundaries. Completion must accept only the desired completion state. Protect ownership and parent IDs. 
Confirm who may change participant edit permissions, including through restore. Add same-company direct-database 
attacks and company-A-admin versus company-B tests.

6. **M2 — Medium — FR-018/020, AC-010/016: persistence requirements contradict each other.**  
   **Scenario (provider failure):** Creating a note from a transcript saves nothing until review under AC-010. If 
generation fails, FR-020 and AC-016 require that nonexistent note and transcript to “stay saved.” Attachment failure 
likewise leaves unclear whether the old or replacement transcript survives.  
   **Evidence:** [AC-010:230](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:230), 
[AC-016:236](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:236), [owner F3 
answer:91](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:91).  
   **Fix:** Obtain an owner decision and specify separate persistence states for new-note generation, attachment 
replacement, and reprocessing. Define what exists before dispatch, after failure/cancellation, and after reviewed 
save; align both ACs.

7. **M3 — Medium — FR-007/008/018, BR-007/011: concurrency and atomicity stop at an unclear boundary.**  
   **Scenario (concurrency/crash):** Transcript replacement races with reprocessing; item editing overwrites an 
assignee’s completion; restore races with editing. A crash can save summary/transcript but omit accepted items or the 
immutable version.  
   **Evidence:** [FR-007:105](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:105). The 
existing [repository 
update:120](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/repositories/implementations/supabase/SupabaseMeetingNoteRepository.ts:120) 
performs an unconditional update and handles items separately.  
   **Fix:** Define revisions for note edits, restore, transcript replacement, AI draft application, and item 
mutations. Require atomic reviewed-save commits and current authorization at commit. Preserve the owner’s 
current-state-only item history policy; explicitly state whether restore leaves the transcript unchanged. Add actual 
competing-transaction coverage.

8. **M4 — Medium — FR-028, BR-005, AC-006/021: “active” and historical membership conflict.**  
   **Scenario (membership removal/restore):** Removal sets `users.company_id = NULL`; it does not set an “inactive” 
membership status. A retained former participant violates BR-005’s blanket active-member requirement, potentially 
preventing later saves or restores. Physical user deletion sets an item’s assignee to NULL, making “Former member” 
indistinguishable from originally unassigned.  
   **Evidence:** [removal migration:770](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260718210827_phase7_company_m
ember_atomic_removal.sql:770), [assignee 
FK:1391](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183000_baseline_core_schema.sql:1391).  
   **Fix:** Define membership through persisted company affiliation, independently of presence status. Restrict *new 
selections* to current members while permitting retained historical placeholders without granting rights. Define 
deleted/rejoined-user handling across versions, restore, and export, and reauthorize in-flight results/saves after 
removal.

9. **M5 — Medium — FR-018/019: reprocessing has no action-item merge contract.**  
   **Scenario (real editor):** A note already has completed/manual items. Saving a regenerated draft could append 
duplicates, replace every existing item, or exceed the 100-item maximum. All are plausible interpretations of “saving 
stores accepted items.”  
   **Evidence:** [FR-018/019:116](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:116), [owner 
reprocessing answer:90](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:90).  
   **Fix:** Record an owner-approved append/reconcile/replace policy, duplicate handling, preservation of existing 
completion state, and behavior when accepted plus existing items exceed 100. Test reprocessing a populated note rather 
than only a new note.

10. **M6 — Medium — BR-009, §10/12, AC-017: key isolation and verification omit important surfaces.**  
    **Scenario (real member/provider error):** Placing encrypted AI credentials in existing `companies.settings` 
exposes that data through normal company reads and direct Supabase SELECT. Masking the new settings response does not 
fix those paths. Raw provider errors can also expose credentials. “No page ever contains the key” contradicts entering 
it in the admin form.  
    **Evidence:** [company 
mapping:14](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/repositories/implementations/supabase/SupabaseCompanyRepository.ts:14), 
[company response:45](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/app/api/companies/get/route.ts:45), [company SELECT 
policy:209](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183139_enable_core_table_rls.sql:209).  
    **Fix:** Require isolated server-only secret storage, outside universally readable settings, with no client 
SELECT/decrypt/Realtime access. Define safe metadata responses. Exempt initial admin entry from the browser 
prohibition; add canary checks for own-company database access, responses, errors, logs, bundles, and Realtime 
payloads.

11. **M7 — Medium — FR-012/016/022, SM-1, §17: accepted size, provider capabilities, and latency are not reconciled.** 
 
    **Scenario (valid upload/admin configuration):** A ≤1 MB transcript exceeds the chosen model’s token budget, 
reasoning consumes the output budget, or a permitted effort value is unsupported. Generation returns truncated JSON or 
misses 60 seconds. OpenAI-compatible transport does not imply identical reasoning controls. 
[OpenAI](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/reasoning), 
[Kimi](https://platform.kimi.ai/docs/guide/use-thinking-models), 
[GLM](https://docs.z.ai/guides/capabilities/thinking).  
    **Evidence:** [SM-1:37](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:37), [provider 
requirement:120](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:120).  
    **Fix:** Require a provider/model capability matrix, validated wire parameters, token preflight including 
prompt/member-list/output budgets, bounded output, and handling of malformed/refused/truncated drafts. Resolve 
oversized-context behavior without silently weakening the approved upload limit. Define the latency fixture, timing 
interval, and deployment deadline. Test all four adapters; AC-022 proves only the tested OpenAI configuration.

12. **M8 — Medium — §14/15 and state readiness claims: AC references do not establish complete coverage.**  
    **Scenario (ordinary use/security attempts):** Tests can pass while private-space creation fails, 
former/cross-company assignees are accepted, history is mutable, or search ignores action-item descriptions.  
    **Evidence:** [ACs:221](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:221), [readiness 
claim:149](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:149).  
    **Fix:** Add explicit assertions for required title/date; supported formatting and full note display; 
private-space creation; editor item edit/delete and unrelated completion denial; assignee eligibility; immutable 
versions and viewer restore denial; per-item review/edit/reassignment; successful usage counting; every search 
field/language/case, pagination and ordering; and malicious AI output through view/export. Define SM-2’s measurement 
environment—local-only AC-014 does not establish an unrestricted performance claim. Use real DB/routes/UI; the 
approved external fake AI server remains permissible.

13. **M9 — Medium — §9/10/16: migration and compatibility obligations are incomplete.**  
    **Scenario (rollout/legacy data):** Changing only the two example fields leaves no creator/backfill contract, 
